1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:01,240
[1949 film] One couple.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,160
[1949 film] That means a date.

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:08,020
[1949 film] Not like just going around with the crowd.

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:10,780
[1949 film] Just me and the girl.

5
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:13,880
[1949 film] Well, that's all right.

6
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:17,560
[1949 film] Only... what girl?

7
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:19,200
[1949 film] Who?

8
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,020
[1949 film] How do you choose a date?

9
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:44,460
[1949 film] Whose company would you enjoy?

10
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:48,060
[1949 film] Well, one thing you can consider is looks.

11
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,120
[1949 film] Woody thought of Janice and how good-looking she was.

12
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:56,600
[1949 film] He'd really have to rate to date somebody like her.

13
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,180
[1949 film] What about Ann?

14
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:02,800
[1949 film] She knows how to have a good time, and how to make the fellow with her relax.

15
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:03,820
[1949 film] Have fun, too.

16
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:07,200
[1949 film] Yes, that's what a boy likes.

17
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,380
[1949 film] He wants to know he's appreciated.

18
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,760
[1949 film] Ann would be fun on a date.

19
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:42,940
[1949 film] Ann? This is Woody.

20
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:48,480
[1949 film] Well, I have a ticket for the Hi-Teen Carnival Saturday, and...

21
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:49,440
[1949 film] Well, would you like to go?

22
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:51,860
[1949 film] Why, yes, Woody.

23
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:54,180
[1949 film] I'll have to talk to my folks about it.

24
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:57,180
[1949 film] But I think I can go. That'll be fine.

25
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:32,340
[1949 film] Well, if you don't overdo on dating...

26
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:36,640
[1949 film] Ed knows what I mean. Weekends only, and not too late.

27
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:40,800
[1949 film] I think the important thing about a date is to have a good time.

28
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:43,740
[1949 film] You don't need to spend a lot of money to do that.

29
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:50,280
[1949 film] You just enjoy whatever you do, whether it's movies or parties or anything.

30
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:53,760
[1949 film] And you leave your boyfriend enough money, so he'll ask you again.

31
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:58,140
[1949 film] Any girl who can't be ready on time for a date isn't good enough for my boy.

32
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:31,720
[1949 film] But how do you say good night?

33
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:34,860
[1949 film] Perhaps...

34
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:38,100
[1949 film] Don't leave!

35
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,860
[1949 film] 1 a.m.

36
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:45,180
[1949 film] Well, so long.

37
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,720
[1949 film] Just like that.

38
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:53,180
[1949 film] After all, a girl likes to know you've had a good time.

39
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:56,040
[1949 film] Well, it's getting late.

40
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,440
[1949 film] Yes, it is.

41
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,180
[1949 film] I'd ask you in for a bite to eat if it weren't so late.

42
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:05,120
[1949 film] Let's plan to get home in time for a sandwich or something next time.

43
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,040
[1949 film] Say, that sounds good.

44
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:08,560
[1949 film] I'll call you next week.

45
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:09,320
[1949 film] Will you?

46
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:12,320
[1949 film] Well, thanks so much.

47
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,820
[1949 film] I had a nice time.

48
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,080
[1949 film] So did I.

49
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:16,300
[1949 film] Good night, Woody.

50
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,340
[1949 film] Night, Ann.

